<section class="hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">FOR TEAMS WHOSE AUDIENCE IS NOT ONE AUDIENCE</p>
  <h1>Real News,<br />Made for One.</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Not a newsletter blasted to a list. Upload your audience and every person
    gets their own issue — real reporting, chosen and written for their role,
    their company and their market. The same coverage publishes to your site
    as a feed and an embed, so your domain keeps producing the topical content
    your audience and search engines come back for.
  </p>
  <p class="price">$25<span>/month</span></p>
  <p>One company. Unlimited recipients. Publish your feed once 10 stakeholders are on board. Cancel future renewals online.</p>
  <form id="login-form" class="signup">
    <label for="email">Work email</label>
    <div class="field-row">
      <input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@company.com" required />
      <button>Start my newsletter →</button>
    </div>
  </form>
  <p class="small">Sign in by email or password. Preview before checkout. No card needed to sign in.</p>
  <p id="message" role="status"></p>
</section>

<section class="grid">
  <article class="card">
    <h2>Stay relevant</h2>
    <p>Your industry moves whether or not you are talking about it. A daily briefing on your market, your competitors and the technologies your buyers care about keeps your team fluent in the conversation their customers are already having.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="card">
    <h2>Build topical authority</h2>
    <p>Every issue also publishes to your domain as hosted stories, a branded RSS feed and an embeddable widget. Consistent, on-topic coverage is what tells readers — and search engines — that your site is a place your subject is actually covered.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="card">
    <h2>Keep readers reading</h2>
    <p>A newsletter people finish is one that opens with something meant for them. That is the whole idea behind the name: one reader, one issue, assembled for them rather than for a list.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <p class="eyebrow">PERSONALISED FOR EVERY READER</p>
  <h2>One audience. A different newsletter each.</h2>
  <p>Upload your list and we enrich it — name, job title, company, industry. Each morning, every reader's issue is assembled for them: the stories chosen and ordered for someone in their role, at a company like theirs, in their market. A VP of Engineering and a Head of Sales at the same company open genuinely different newsletters.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Industry, competitor and keyword coverage you choose</li>
    <li>Stories selected per reader from their role, company and market</li>
    <li>Original write-ups of each story, crediting and linking the publisher</li>
    <li>Unlimited confirmed recipients — no per-seat pricing</li>
    <li>A branded feed, an embeddable widget and hosted stories on your site</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="small">Summaries are based on available source material and may contain errors. Original reporting remains with the linked publishers.</p>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <p class="eyebrow">HOW THE PRICE STAYS AT $25</p>
  <h2>Sponsored stories pay for the rest.</h2>
  <p>Each issue carries a clearly marked sponsored story and a small number of ad placements, sold and served by Rnews1. That advertising is what keeps a fully personalised newsletter at a flat $25 a month however large your audience grows.</p>
  <p class="small">Sponsored placements are always labelled and never presented as your own editorial. Advertisers can target by professional role and industry, so a reader sees advertising relevant to their job rather than the same generic banner as everyone else. Your list is never sold or shared, and advertisers never see who received their ad. If you need ad-free issues under your own branding, that is what the enterprise plan is for.</p>
</section>

<section class="grid">
  <article class="card">
    <h2>Is this another newsletter tool?</h2>
    <p>Newsletter tools send what you write. Rnews1 writes it — you choose the topics and upload the audience, and the issues arrive every morning without anyone on your team drafting one.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="card">
    <h2>What happens after signup?</h2>
    <p>Confirm your email, enter your company domain, choose your topics, preview the coverage, then activate your $25/month subscription. Add 10 stakeholders from your company and your feed goes live.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="card">
    <h2>Need a custom deployment?</h2>
    <p>Enterprise engagements start at $10,000, subject to scope: ad-free issues, dedicated hosting, custom domains, unbranded embeds, your own sponsors, and advanced exclusions.</p>
